|~ `::tag`, the kind of a tag name, and what is declared under it: its
   constructor and its refusal, the comparisons of tag names, the verbs
   that turn a tag name into a string and a keyword, and `toTag`, which
   answers the tag itself.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:tag
  |~~ A tag names a kind, and a value carries its kind as the tag over
      it: `[1 2]` is of `::vec`, `::Box[1 2]` a vector under `::Box`.
      Taken alone, `::Box` is a value of this kind, the name a query
      asks about the kind: `::vec | doc` reads its page and
      `::vec | manifest` lists what lies under it, and `type` answers
      the tag of any value, `[1 2] | type` answering `::vec`.

      It is written `::` and a name, a slash joining names into an
      address, `::vec/count`; a tag that touches a payload puts the
      payload under it, which ::link~(::tagged | doc) tells. A label is a
      kind declared under a name, by the chain that builds it from
      ::link~(::kind | doc) or by its page alone, and its tag is the
      address of that name; a tag nothing declares is a kind of identity,
      which checks nothing and lays itself over the value. Tags rank after
      keywords and before paths, and JSON writes a tag as its literal,
      `"::Box"`.
      ::snippet~(kinds) lists the kinds the scope reads, and
      ::snippet~(::Box::Crate{:a 1} | type) answers the outer tag.
      ::link~(::qlang/values | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps |~~ A tag name, read as itself. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
            tag is read by `type`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isATag
        |~~ A tag name is a value of `::tag`. ~~|
        ~(::Box | type | eq ::tag)
    | proves :namesAPage
        |~~ The tag of a kind names its page. ~~|
        ~(5 | type | doc | type | eq ::doc)
    | proves :namesNothingUndeclared
        |~~ A tag no declaration answers names no record. ~~|
        ~(::Unbound[1] | type | binding !| type | eq ::any/binding/UnknownNameError)
    | proves :readsATagNameAsItself
        |~~ `::tag` over a tag name is that name. ~~|
        ~(::tag::Box | eq ::Box)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAKeyword
        |~~ A keyword payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(::tag:k !| get [~(type) /actualType] | eq [::tag/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::keyword])
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/gt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives, `::b | gt ::a`. Tag names compare by their names as
      they are spelled, letter by letter, so a capital comes before a
      small letter, `::a | gt ::B` answering `true`, and a name comes
      before the names that go on under it, `::vec/count | gt ::vec`
      answering `true`; values sorted by `type` so fall in the order of
      the names of their kinds. A tag name compares with a tag name
      alone: a keyword, a string or any other value given is refused
      under the value, `::status | gt :open` among them. `gte` answers
      whether the subject comes after the value or is the same name,
      `lt` and `lte` the reverse.
      ::link~(::tag/gte | doc) ::link~(::tag/lt | doc)
      ::link~(::tag/lte | doc) ::link~(::keyword/gt | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | gt ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gt ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `gt` of keywords, `:b | gt :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value, `false`
            otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | proves :ordersByName |~~ `::b` comes after `::a`. ~~| ~(::b | gt ::a)
    | proves :putsACapitalFirst
        |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~|
        ~(::a | gt ::B)
    | proves :putsANameBeforeTheNamesUnderIt
        |~~ A name comes before the names that go on under it. ~~|
        ~(::vec/count | gt ::vec)
    | proves :keepsOneNameApartFromItself
        |~~ A name does not come after itself. ~~|
        ~(::a | gt ::a | not)
    | proves :ordersValuesByTheNamesOfTheirKinds
        |~~ Values sorted by `type` fall in the order of the names of
            their kinds.
        ~~|
        ~([1 "a" :k] | sort ~(type) | eq [:k 1 "a"])
    | proves :value/KindNotTakenError/refusesAKeyword
        |~~ A keyword is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::a | gt :a !| type | eq ::tag/gt/value/KindNotTakenError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/gte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::b | gte ::b`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names, by their names as they are
      spelled.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | gte ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gte ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `gte` of keywords, `:b | gte :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value or is the same
            name, `false` otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | proves :holdsOfItself
        |~~ A name comes after or is itself. ~~|
        ~(::b | gte ::b)
    | proves :keepsAnEarlierNameApart
        |~~ An earlier name does not come after a later one. ~~|
        ~(::a | gte ::b | not)
    | proves :value/KindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | gte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/gte/value/KindNotTakenError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/lt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives, `::a | lt ::b`. It compares as `gt` does, tag names
      with tag names, by their names as they are spelled, so
      `::B | lt ::a` answers `true`.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | lt ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lt ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `lt` of keywords, `:b | lt :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value, `false`
            otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | proves :ordersByName |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~| ~(::a | lt ::b)
    | proves :putsACapitalFirst
        |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~|
        ~(::B | lt ::a)
    | proves :keepsOneNameApartFromItself
        |~~ A name does not come before itself. ~~|
        ~(::a | lt ::a | not)
    | proves :value/KindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | lt 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lt/value/KindNotTakenError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/lte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::a | lte ::a`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names.
      ::link~(::tag/lt | doc) ::link~(::tag/gte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | lte ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lte ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `lte` of keywords, `:b | lte :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value or is the same
            name, `false` otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | proves :holdsOfItself
        |~~ A name comes before or is itself. ~~|
        ~(::a | lte ::a)
    | proves :ordersByName
        |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~|
        ~(::a | lte ::b)
    | proves :value/KindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | lte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lte/value/KindNotTakenError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toString
  |~~ Answers the name of the tag as a string, `::vec | toString`
      answering `"vec"`, so a kind joins text. `toTag` turns the name
      back into the tag.
      ::link~(::string/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The name of the tag, a string. ~~| ::string
    | proves :answersTheName
        |~~ A tag answers its name. ~~|
        ~([::vec ::number/add] | map ~toString | eq ["vec" "number/add"])
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toKeyword
  |~~ Answers the keyword of the tag's name, `::Box | toKeyword`
      answering `:Box`, as `groupBy ~(type)` files values by their kinds.
      `toTag` turns the keyword back into the tag.
      ::link~(::keyword/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The keyword of the tag's name. ~~| ::keyword
    | proves :readsBack
        |~~ A tag turned into its keyword turns back into itself. ~~|
        ~(::Box | toKeyword | toTag | eq ::Box)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toTag
  |~~ Answers the tag itself, so `map ~toTag` turns names and tags into
      tags, `["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag` answering
      `[::vec ::Box ::map]`.
      ::link~(::string/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The tag itself. ~~| ::tag
    | proves :answersItself
        |~~ A tag answers itself, so names and tags turn into tags. ~~|
        ~(["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag | eq [::vec ::Box ::map])
    | impl ::builtin{}

